  "articleBody": "Thinking about installing a new door frame in your basement but wondering if it’s a DIY job or if you should call in the pros? It really depends on a few key things. You might want to consider professional help if: The opening isn't square: If your rough opening isn’t perfectly square, getting a pre-hung door frame to fit properly can be a real challenge. Pros have techniques like scribing and careful shimming to make it work. The foundation or framing is irregular: Basements can have unique structural quirks. If you’re dealing with an uneven foundation or odd framing, it takes experience to adjust the frame without compromising its integrity. The frame must align with other finish carpentry: If your door frame needs to seamlessly blend with existing trim or other finish work, precision is paramount. A professional can ensure all lines flow perfectly together. You want a perfect, gap-free fit: Achieving a perfectly plumb, level, and square door frame with tight joints and no gaps takes practice and specialized tools. If you’re aiming for a flawless finish, a professional will deliver. In these situations, calling in HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of headaches and ensure your basement door looks and functions exactly as it should. We’ve got the know-how to handle tricky installations and deliver a high-quality result.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
